.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-SET-KEY-DESCRIPTION 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-set-key-description \- change what a key says it is for
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm set-key-description
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I ERN
.BR \-\-description | \-d
.I TEXT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces a key's description.
.PP
A key is identified by a generated ID which says nothing about what it
protects. The description is what does \- and what answers, months
later when somebody is deciding whether a key can be deleted, what
would be lost with it.
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1)
takes one; this is how it is corrected afterwards.
.PP
Worth correcting rather than leaving: a key that has been revoked or
scheduled for deletion is exactly the kind whose description should say
why, and it is the last thing anyone reads before
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1)
makes the decision permanent.
.PP
Only the description changes. The key material, algorithm, length,
status and any scheduled deletion are untouched, so describing a key
neither prolongs nor shortens its life, and a key that cannot encrypt
still cannot after being described.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the key. Required. Named by ERN, as
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1)
names it \-
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1)
prints both the ERN and the ID.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fITEXT\fR
What the key is for. Free text, never interpreted. Required, but may be
empty: passing
.I ""
clears the description rather than leaving it alone, since otherwise
there would be no way to remove one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The description was set. The key's ERN, ID and new description are
printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, no session, or no key with that ERN.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ekm set-key-description \e
    --key ern:ekm:eu-central-1:000000000000:key:9f2c1e40 \e
    --description "payroll exports, rotated quarterly"
.fi
.RE
.PP
prints
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"ern":"ern:ekm:eu-central-1:000000000000:key:9f2c1e40",
 "name":"9f2c1e40",
 "description":"payroll exports, rotated quarterly"}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clearing a description:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ekm set-key-description \e
    --key ern:ekm:eu-central-1:000000000000:key:9f2c1e40 \e
    --description ""
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1)
